MDL110, K19, F1, F12: "key[bar baz]=1" is not a valid GLib key name (a '['
may only start a locale suffix of letters, digits, '-', '_', '.' and '@'), so
GLib rejects the file: mydumper ignores all of it, connects through [client],
exits 0 and dumps users.email in plaintext. The line also starts a bracket
state leak (MDL112): an empty line after it would break the file as well.
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.1-1
args: --defaults-file /work/defaults.cnf --database app
lint: MDL110, MDL112, MDL405
when < v0.19.3-1
# No pre-processor before v0.19.3-1, hence no bracket state leak (MDL112).
lint: MDL110, MDL405
end
expect config-loaded: false
expect stderr-contains: Invalid key name
expect exit: 0
expect connected: true
expect column app.users.email: plaintext
-- defaults.cnf --
[client]
host=mysql
user=e2e
password=e2e-password

[mydumper]
threads=2
key[bar baz]=1
[`app`.`users`]
`email`=random_string
